  "worked_solution": "Recall that \"The square root of $1\\,024$ is a natural number\" means the following:\n\nThere exists a natural number $n$ such that $\\sqrt{1\\,024}=n.$\n\nMore formally, this reads as follows:\n\n$∃\\,n\\in N,\\,\\sqrt{1\\,024}=n$",
